From 1a2d4b105d9dd936f087a42a03d55cd4b398d042 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:21:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.9.9: Backup & Restore redesign + full i18n review pass

1. Reaper_Backup.asp rebuilt to the owner-approved theme design: scythe
   sigil header with live model/version//jffs chips, a three-step restore
   lifecycle strip whose step 03 arms while a restore is pending, tiered
   vault layout (full-backup hero + JSON card, then the stock .CFG/JFFS
   stores), factory reset quarantined behind a hazard stripe, film grain +
   vignette. All v2.9.8 behavior unchanged. New tokens RBKP_27-32.

2. i18n review across every Reaper page (4-audit pass):
   - 9 wrong-token labels fixed on Reaper_Firewall.asp: Protocol and
     Schedule columns/inputs on the Egress, Forwards and Service Intercept
     cards were labeled with the Outbound/Forwarded direction tokens.
   - Hardcoded English tokenized: Warden save-error alert, Devices lease
     badge + HTML-export title/headers, dashboard N-core label, Conn error
     fallback, Wireless report score header, VPN Routing object-type words,
     Firewall log-mode value + log-class badges, QoS class-name fallback.
     New tokens RDEV_93-95, RDSH_90, RWDN_101.
   - EN copy fixes: RFW_245 possessive, RFW_240 clause, RFW_207 Deny->Drop
     terminology, RWDN_18, RABT_35, RQOS_08; 28 stock ASUS typo instances
     corrected (Randsomware, authentification, Encyption, PROCOTOL, ...).
   - Translation fill: 57 never-translated Reaper tokens + all partially
     translated stragglers now localized in all 24 non-EN languages,
     matching each dictionary's established terminology. Deliberately kept
     English: threat-feed proper names (FireHOL Level 1, Spamhaus DROP) and
     tokens whose English form is the native technical term per dict.
   All 25 dictionaries lockstep at 6803 lines; langcheck + csrfcheck clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
