-RABT_17=Creator and maintainer of Asuswrt-Merlin, the firmware every line of this build is patched on top of. Reaper is a fork with opinions; this is the thing it has opinions about. Remove him from the picture and there is no picture.
-RABT_18=Compile-integrity guidance, and a bug hunter with a genuinely unsettling hit rate. If a build was going to fall over, he tended to know before the build did.
-RABT_19=The QA department nobody hired, nobody budgeted for, and nobody can now imagine shipping a release without.
-RABT_20=Brought real operational experience to the reporting thread and quietly filtered the noise out of it. Half the value of a bug report is knowing it is a bug.
-RABT_21=Speaks quietly and infrequently. Every single time, it was worth stopping what I was doing to read it.
-RABT_22=Never once let a test build go untested. GT-BE98 owners have working firmware because these two kept flashing it and saying what happened.
-RABT_23=Sole, tireless and remarkably patient ambassador for the RT-BE88U. That model is in far better shape for it.
